<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia building approvals rise in April.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia building approvals rise in April.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian dwelling unit building approvals rose a seasonally-adjusted 3.6 percent in April to 11,781 from 11,368 in March, compared with 10,379 in April 1996, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The bureau said approvals for private sector houses rose 11 percent in April.</p>
<p>Economists on average had expected building approvals to rise 3.0 percent.  </p>
<p>Australian housing building approvals-</p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJUSTED		 April 97  March 97 April 96</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  8,268    7,448    7,324</p>
<p>    Total houses			     8,159    7,678    7,314</p>
<p>    Total private dwelling units	11,796   10,895    9,728</p>
<p>    Total dwelling units		  11,781   11,368   10,379</p>
<p>    Value residential building (A$ bln) 1.48     1.26     1.20</p>
<p>    Value total buildings (A$ bln)	2.04     2.19     2.11</p>
<p>TREND ESTIMATES</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  7,812     7,666    7,087</p>
<p>    Total Dwelling Units		  11,692    11,672   10,376</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted estimate for the volatile other residential dwelling unit sector fell 1.8 percent in April, following a fall of 13.4 percent in March.</p>
<p>The bureau said the Olympics game village has not yet been included and notification would be given when it is included.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
